[h1]Random New World 1.2.1[/h1]

A hotfix for 1.2.0: the countries of a generated New World no longer each trade in a market of their own. For EU5 1.4.7.

[h2]🔧 Fixes and improvements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Fixed almost every country of the New World getting its own market. 1.2.0 made each country with a recorded exchange agreement a market centre and a town, so 70–87 % of the capitals held a market (115 market centres for 127 countries in one world). The game's Americas have 12 for 223 countries. Market centres and towns are placed by the settlement plan again: the cities, the largest state near each hearth and one local market for each group of countries that no market reaches (18 in that world).
[*]The check before generation asks for about 9 GB of free RAM, the measured need of a 1.2.0 world, and says how much is free if it stops.
[/list]

[quote][b]Updating:[/b] For EU5 1.4.7. Generate a new world to get the corrected markets; keep the original world mod for existing saves. World Codes from 1.2.0 can give different worlds in 1.2.1 (algorithm epoch 62), and such worlds cannot be rerolled by part. Use one RNW world at a time and restart EU5 when switching maps.[/quote]

